=== task: cells easy
title: The front after each step
prompt: A queue starts empty. Which item is at the front after each step?
labels: enqueue 5 | enqueue 7 | dequeue | enqueue 2
answer: 5 | 5 | 7 | 7
wrong[5 | 7 | 5 | 2]: That's how a stack's top behaves. A queue's front stays the same while items join behind it.
wrong[5 | 5 | 7 | 2]: Enqueue adds at the back: the 2 goes behind the 7, which is still at the front.
